# ...but keep the dependency list tracked.
!07_reconstruction/requirements.txt

# Slurm job-submission folders (per-run worker scripts, work queues, job-id records)
**/slurm/

# Cloned reference implementations (RND paper repo, CleanRL, ExPLORe) — large, not tracked
reference_repos/
# The untouched upstream CleanRL clone (255 MB, carries its own .git). Its URL and commit hash are
# recorded in 08_cleanrl_ppo_rnd/UPSTREAM.md, which IS tracked; the modified training code lives in
# the tracked 08_cleanrl_ppo_rnd/src/.
08_cleanrl_ppo_rnd/cleanrl/
# A pip package tree installed into the benchmark scratch folder while profiling (980 MB of it).
# The benchmark scripts and their result JSONs next to it stay tracked.
08_cleanrl_ppo_rnd/bench_scratch/envpool_pkgs/
# Inductor's compilation cache (regenerable, and only used when torch.compile is on).
08_cleanrl_ppo_rnd/.torchinductor_cache/
# The ExPLORe clone that used to sit at the repo root was deleted 2026-07-22; the one kept copy is
# /p/rlprojects/RLforOR/accelerating_exploration_with_unlabeled_prior_data/explore. This keeps a
# future re-clone here out of git (the existing "explore/" line above only covers the lowercase name).
/ExPLORe/

# Optuna controller state inside a run folder (journal log, per-trial decisions, SWEEP_COMPLETE
# sentinel) — regenerable run state, same treatment as the slurm/ and queue/ folders. The tutorial
# folder 07_reconstruction/optuna/ is NOT covered by this and stays tracked.
07_reconstruction/train_runs/**/optuna/

# Work-queue folders inside a run folder (pending/running/done/failed job configs)
07_reconstruction/train_runs/**/queue/

# jaguar03 threading experiment (inside the run-5 folder): measurement outputs, regenerable by
# re-running the experiment scripts. avxburn_work/ holds one .w text file per hardware thread
# (time + throughput lines); load_sweep_work/ holds per-worker .txt outputs; the data*/ folders
# hold the collected sweep measurements. The code files next to them (run_experiment.py,
# load_sweep.py, avxburn.c, jaguar03_throttle_repro.sh, report.md) stay tracked.
07_reconstruction/train_runs/**/jaguar03_threading_experiment/avxburn_work/
07_reconstruction/train_runs/**/jaguar03_threading_experiment/load_sweep_work/
07_reconstruction/train_runs/**/jaguar03_threading_experiment/data_*/

# Lock files written next to the collaborator job-id files while a worker appends to them
*.lock

# Optuna / sqlite storage backends
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Monitoring snapshots inside a run folder (per-tick table dumps; the scripts themselves stay tracked)
07_reconstruction/train_runs/**/20_mins_monitoring/outputs/

# Analysis folders (any project): code and data are scratch; plots and analysis.md are the durable
# record and must survive the blanket *.pdf / *.json / *.png rules above, hence the negations.
# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to this file's directory, so it needs the leading **/ to
# reach 08_cleanrl_ppo_rnd/train_runs/... as well as a top-level train_runs/.
**/train_runs/**/analysis/code/
**/train_runs/**/analysis/data/
!**/analysis/plots/
!**/analysis/plots/*.pdf
!**/analysis/plots/*.png
!**/analysis/*.tex

# 09_parallelization: reference clones and the unzipped external skill (external content, not versioned here)
09_parallelization/reference_repo/
09_parallelization/parallel_agents_skill/
# keep the validation fixtures (small, regenerable, but they anchor all GPU env checks)
!09_parallelization/pointmaze/common/fixtures/*.npz
!09_parallelization/pointmaze/common/fixtures/*.json

# Core dumps written beside a crashed training job — gigabytes each, never wanted in git
core.*

# Reference repositories cloned inside an analysis folder for comparison. They carry their own
# .git, so committing them would nest one repository inside another; clone them again if needed.
**/reference_autoresearch/
**/reference_repos/

# 10_jax_exploration_platform.
# The `env/` rule near the top of this file (meant for a python virtual environment) also hides
# the platform's `configs/env/` and `benchmarks/env/` folders, which hold code and must be tracked.
!10_jax_exploration_platform/configs/env/
!10_jax_exploration_platform/benchmarks/env/
# A run folder's launch command is part of its permanent record; the blanket `*.txt` rule above
# would drop it. The run's data shards (`data/*.jsonl`), its aggregated `metrics.jsonl`, its
# `summary.json` and its `logs/` stay ignored — all four are regenerable from the shards, and the
# shards themselves are large. `manifest.yaml`, `config_resolved.yaml` and
# `experiment_background.md` are already tracked by the rules above.
!10_jax_exploration_platform/runs/**/command.txt
!10_jax_exploration_platform/benchmark_runs/**/command.txt
# A research round's `result.json` is the round's permanent record — the few numbers its verdict
# rests on, small, and useless to regenerate because the card and the session it was measured in
# are gone. The raw benchmark output it was assembled from stays ignored under `benchmark_runs/`.
!10_jax_exploration_platform/research/**/result.json
# A run's submission plan and its own rate measurements are part of its permanent record: the plan
# says which cards each work unit was sent to and what every rejected alternative would have cost,
# and the measurements are what priced it. Both are small, and neither can be regenerated — the
# cards that were free and the machines the rates were measured on are gone by the next day.
!10_jax_exploration_platform/runs/**/code/submission_plan.json
!10_jax_exploration_platform/runs/**/code/measured_cells.json
# A platform run's canary folder: throwaway short runs that prove the card, the compiled-program
# cache and the resume before the real submission. Its numbers live in the run's own
# canary_estimate_vs_actual.md, which IS tracked.
10_jax_exploration_platform/runs/**/canary/
# A platform run's rate-probe folder: short runs that measure the arms at each copy count the
# submission plan might choose. Its numbers live in the run's code/measured_cells.json, which IS
# tracked; the folder itself is scratch, like canary/.
10_jax_exploration_platform/runs/**/probe/

# 11_decay_rate: the cloned reference repo (karpathy/autoresearch, kept for reference only) and
# the iteration-loop experiment outputs (per-experiment JSON records + plots, regenerable from
# method.py at the logged commit; the tracked ledger is 11_decay_rate/results.tsv).
11_decay_rate/autoresearch/
# code/slurm/ holds SUBMISSION SCRIPTS (not job output) — un-hide it from **/slurm/
!11_decay_rate/code/slurm/
# experiments/: ignore records and logs but keep each campaign's launch-time identity files
# (a bare directory exclude would stop git descending, so the negations below need the /* form)
11_decay_rate/experiments/*
!11_decay_rate/experiments/*/
11_decay_rate/experiments/*/*
!11_decay_rate/experiments/*/experiment_background.md
!11_decay_rate/experiments/*/manifest.yaml
!11_decay_rate/experiments/*/command.txt
